WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.450
- When we think about our life,

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:05.036
we usually think about
it in a form of a story.

00:00:05.036 --> 00:00:05.869
(slow music)

00:00:05.869 --> 00:00:07.800
First we were born and
then we did some things

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.610
and made some memories and now we're here

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.200
and we work at our job or whatever.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.170
But in the future we plan
on doing more things,

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.100
seeing the world maybe
and saving up enough money

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.300
for a enjoyable retirement.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.020
We all tend to view our lives

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.530
in a sort of narrative
structure like this,

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.280
with the beginning, a
middle and an eventual end.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.210
Which kinda makes sense because
by reflecting on the past,

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.120
it helps us make sense of where we are now

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.840
and by having hopes and
dreams for the future,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.900
it gives us something to look forward to,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.610
something to plan towards

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:43.480
and if we currently don't
like our present situation,

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.260
we can place our pains and
frustrations on the hope

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:47.200
of a better tomorrow.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.190
But if you think about what it feels like

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.560
to actually live life,
like what it feels like

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:55.780
on a day to day basis, it
feels completely different.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.240
We kinda just wake up,
we feel kinda groggy,

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.350
we stumble downstairs, get the coffee,

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.640
hop in the shower, you
get dressed before getting

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.330
in the car to get that bread.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.690
And after you get that bread,

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.610
you get more bread at McDonald's

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:08.900
because you have an addiction

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.830
and then you come home,
usually pretty tired

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:14.220
and you veg out and watch
Netflix or whatever you do

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.290
until you go to bed.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:18.030
This is what living
life usually feels like

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.950
to most people most of the time.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:23.050
Life in general is usually pretty normal.

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:24.860
You do the things that you do everyday,

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.350
you kinda have a routine
or a pattern you stick to

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:31.230
and life usually isn't super
inspiring or mind-blowing,

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.810
it's just sort of the
day to day experience.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.910
But is there anything wrong with that?

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.800
I mean, social media has us thinking

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.190
that everyone's hanging
out on yachts all the time,

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:41.860
going on crazy adventures,

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:45.330
trying out the 2,000 different
bananas in southeast Asia

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:46.810
and everyone's getting married

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.380
to the person of their dreams,

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.400
popping out the most beautiful babies.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.050
But that's not life,
that's a highlight reel.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.830
And these highlights
that we constantly absorb

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.580
by the people we follow on
Instagram or the movies we watch

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:00.350
on Netflix, these highlights start

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.210
to really influence the
story we tell ourselves

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:04.430
about our own lives.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:07.470
We start viewing our
lives, at least our lives

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.460
lived to it's fullest potential

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:11.820
as a life with as many of these highlights

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.540
in it as possible, so the
days when these awesome,

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.410
crazy things aren't happening,

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:19.070
we view that as somehow suboptimal.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:22.260
Our amazing days become the expectation

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:25.860
and our normal days become
boring, like we're wasting

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.200
our potential, we're
wasting our lives away.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.370
But this story we tell
ourselves, this adventure life,

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.150
no one's life is like this,

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.470
not Dwayne Johnson, not Elon Musk.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:39.160
Sure, these guys are
doing some really cool,

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.870
important things more often than we are

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.270
but still the majority of their lives,

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:46.860
they just sort of wake up,
they do a bunch of things

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.120
they don't wanna do,
they're grinding it out,

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:52.570
they're working hard, they're
often really frustrated

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:53.520
or stressed out.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.890
They still poop, they still have to eat.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:57.950
Most of their lives exist

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.930
in this sort of day to day monotony.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:01.250
They're experiencing life

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:03.260
in the exact same way that you are,

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.370
except when Elon Musk is fantasizing

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.360
about escaping the day to day
grind and taking a vacation,

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.770
instead of the Bahamas,
he's thinking Mars.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.160
Assuming you get eight
hours of sleep every night,

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.930
which I'm sure you do, you only
have about 16 hours to live

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.630
because you only experience
life one day at a time.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.250
That little section of time
between lifting your head

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:24.820
off the pillow and
putting it back down again

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:28.450
and all that stuff in between
that seems kind of normal

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:32.120
and kinda inconsequential,
that's all life is,

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:35.410
it's just that thing over
and over and over again.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:38.990
And this can sound super
depressing or super inspiring,

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:40.480
depending on how you look at it.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.730
It can be depressing,
obviously if you don't like

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:47.500
those 16 hours, usually,
a lot of us are slaves

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:48.810
to our bad habits.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.840
We do things we don't want to do.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:52.720
We work jobs we don't really like

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.740
and we're put in certain
financial or social situations

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:58.010
that we really don't like being in.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.400
So every single day, day after day

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.820
is something we generally
don't like doing.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:05.290
Which is why we fantasize
about the future so much.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.930
We're still waiting to live our real lives

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.882
and if this is all there is,

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.420
then that's obviously super depressing.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:13.620
But there's a silver lining

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.520
because changing your entire life

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.210
isn't as big of a feat
as you might think it is.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:21.160
Since life is lived in
these little 16 hour

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.330
little mini episodes, that's
a very manageable amount

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.530
of time to perfect.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:28.530
We can start to build habits
that we actually enjoy doing

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:29.710
and that are good for us

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:31.840
and we can train ourselves to make choices

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:33.900
that are actually aligned with our values

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.320
and will help us be the person

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.180
we want to be every single day.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:40.610
Because a good life is just
a serious of good days,

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:43.250
not necessarily days where
everything went our way

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.300
and nothing was difficult or stressful

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.400
but days where our system was running.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:51.470
We gave life a good shot, we
made choices that are aligned

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.610
with our values and we
did the little things

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:54.780
that make us happy.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:57.120
Maybe that's having a good
conversation with a friend

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.710
or putting a little extra
effort into cooking,

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:02.070
so you eat something kinda memorable

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.070
and that you're proud of,

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:06.350
maybe that's developing one
positive habit at a time

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:09.190
so that the things that
keep you grounded and happy

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:10.960
and your mood elevated,

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.530
start to become things
that you do automatically.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:16.190
Viewing life on a micro scale like this

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.480
also adds clarity to the little choices

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.690
we make throughout the day.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:22.369
If you've always wanted to
be a more social person,

00:05:22.369 --> 00:05:25.720
then that means saying yes
to beers with the boys today,

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:26.920
when you get the invitation.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.760
And if you're constantly fantasizing

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.830
about being a more fit person,

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.740
that means going to the gym today.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:35.870
Because your life is
today, that's all it is.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.957
It's just today repeated.

